{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And when a soul, etc.</b> In Torat Kohanim they expounded the extra word ״וְנֶפֶשׁ״ as involving a limitation and an expansion: limitation in ״נֶפֶשׁ״ — singular language — to exclude the community, that they should not bring a freewill meal offering; expansion in the extra ו״ו — to include an individual who does not bring an offering for defilement of the Sanctuary and its holy things, namely the anointed priest, who brings a freewill meal offering." "The reason the verse wrote here an expansion and a limitation within a single word is perhaps that, since there was no need to exclude the community except by virtue of the fact that it included the anointed priest, therefore it hinted at both of them together, even though they are two opposite things. For were it not for the inclusion of the anointed priest, there would be no need to exclude the community — for how would it have occurred to us that they bring, such that exclusion would be necessary? And once the inclusion of the anointed priest emerges, a new ruling results for us that is taught regarding the community, as they stated there in Torat Kohanim; therefore it became necessary to exclude."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:52:42.095728701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}